# I'll Be Back, verse, the six-bar phrase: two vocal parts in thirds over a descending bass
# (figure 19.2). Pollack's suspension figures (6-5 over 4-3, and 6-5-4-5 over 4-3-2-3) go under the
# chord row; he notates one chord per bar on purpose, since the bass holds through the suspension.
# Bar 4: the four figures mark the four beats, so the last beat holds two eighths (B C# / G# A).
# Elsewhere notes share the bar equally. The parenthesized C# and A over the final A chord are
# kept as notes (Pollack brackets them as implied).
#? Octaves: the vocal parts are placed around middle C (soprano C4-E4, alto A3-C4), bass A2 down
#? to E2; the voices may sit an octave higher.
key a

